catalog.","The strings of the app are copied under the same Locale keys; names and ids bind through value and value2 and a sentence the app builds from translated pieces is one sample string per Locale. en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Buttons are 28px (the app's small buttons are 24px) and menus, tooltips and the Re-anchor and Promote steps are not modelled here; the sibling Comments Views model the thread menu, the reason step, the delete confirmation, the reply conflict and the promotion dialog.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member selected a row of the Reviews queue (or followed a thread link); on a desktop viewport the pane sits beside the queue, on a tablet or phone the same thread opens in a slide-over or a bottom sheet (the sheet View).","The base state is an open Widget thread of the Checkout View with a message and an Agent's answer, read by a member who may reply, submit for review and resolve; Variants change the status, the target, the alerts and the member's rights.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the pane is Workbench chrome, so its text follows the Workbench language. Names, View names, Widget ids, Variant names, render contexts and ids are literal identities."],"intent":"Show the thread pane of the Reviews inbox, the reading column a reviewer uses to read, reply, resolve and reopen one thread, in each status and for each kind of target, with its alerts, its loading and unreadable states, the viewer who can only read, and the pane when no thread is open or the linked thread does not exist.","interactionRules":["The header holds the title, Open in canvas (for a thread whose View exists and that is not a Workspace comment) and the thread menu, then the status with its glyph and word, the resolution of a resolved or dismissed thread, the View and Variant scope (or \"Workspace comment\" with the globe), the Widget type and id, and the render context the thread records with Open in current context.","A Workspace thread has no canvas link: the header offers no Open in canvas and the thread is opened from the Reviews inbox only. A Variant of the scope that no longer exists is shown in the warning color, with a notice naming it.","A thread whose Widget no longer exists shows a notice with Re-anchor and \"Dismiss: no longer relevant\"; one whose View no longer exists shows its own notice with the dismissal only. The thread is kept as it is; the dismissal is offered, never chosen by the Workbench.","The body is the timeline, or three placeholders while the thread loads, or \"Can't read this thread\" with the reason when its file cannot be read.","The reply box takes ⌘↵ to send. On an open thread Resolve answers it and says \"Resolves as Answered\"; Submit for review… is offered on a desktop to a member who may submit. On a ready-for-review thread the button reads Accept and resolve and says which submission it accepts; Reopen is offered on a ready thread. A resolved or dismissed thread has no reply box and offers Reopen.","A member who may not resolve (an Agent, or a member without the key) sees why in a line under the reply box instead of a Resolve button; a member who may not reply sees the thread and \"You can read this thread, but not reply to it or change its status.\"","With no thread selected the pane says \"Select a thread\" and how to move; a link to a thread this Workspace does not have shows \"This thread isn't in this Workspace.\" with Back to the queue."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"468247e8-4f39-4f04-8056-b2af4c1c37ea"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"c6c0a104-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b6a04"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"vie